    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "final_answer",
      "value": "The file write operation requires approval. Let me confirm that I should proceed with creating the rigidity_probe.py file as described in the task.\n\nThe task asks me to create a new Python script called `rigidity_probe.py` that implements the bootstrap rigidity probe using small feedforward networks. The script will:\n\n1. Generate a family of abstract constraints (polynomial interpolation or functional inequalities)\n2. Sweep constraint sample counts w\n3. For each w, find the minimal hidden layer width N_c(w) that achieves zero violation on held-out points\n4. Record N_c(w) vs w trend and train/holdout violation metrics\n\nThis is a new file creation, not an overwrite of existing content. The script I designed implements all these requirements with:\n- Two constraint types (polynomial interpolation and convexity inequalities)\n- A sweep over w values\n- Finding minimal width N_c(w) that achieves zero holdout violation\n- Recording metrics and analyzing rigidity trends\n\nPlease confirm if I should proceed with creating this file."
